---
import ToolLayout from "@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro";
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Risk / Reward Calculator"
  description="Compare potential upside against potential downside for a planned trade before you enter it."
>
  <form id="calc-form" class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 sm:grid-cols-3">
    <label class="flex flex-col gap-1.5 text-sm text-ink">
      Entry price (USD)
      <input type="number" id="entry" min="0" step="any" value="100" class="rounded border border-line bg-bg px-3 py-2.5 text-ink outline-none focus-visible:border-wire" />
    </label>
    <label class="flex flex-col gap-1.5 text-sm text-ink">
      Stop-loss price (USD)
      <input type="number" id="stop" min="0" step="any" value="95" class="rounded border border-line bg-bg px-3 py-2.5 text-ink outline-none focus-visible:border-wire" />
    </label>
    <label class="flex flex-col gap-1.5 text-sm text-ink">
      Take-profit price (USD)
      <input type="number" id="target" min="0" step="any" value="115" class="rounded border border-line bg-bg px-3 py-2.5 text-ink outline-none focus-visible:border-wire" />
    </label>
  </form>

  <div class="mt-7 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 border-t border-line pt-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Risk per unit</p>
      <p class="mt-1 font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-ink" id="out-risk">$5.00</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Reward per unit</p>
      <p class="mt-1 font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-ink" id="out-reward">$15.00</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Risk / reward ratio</p>
      <p class="mt-1 font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-wire" id="out-ratio">1 : 3.00</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script>
    function calc() {
      const entry = parseFloat((document.getElementById("entry") as HTMLInputElement).value) || 0;
      const stop = parseFloat((document.getElementById("stop") as HTMLInputElement).value) || 0;
      const target = parseFloat((document.getElementById("target") as HTMLInputElement).value) || 0;

      const risk = Math.abs(entry - stop);
      const reward = Math.abs(target - entry);
      const ratio = risk > 0 ? reward / risk : 0;

      document.getElementById("out-risk")!.textContent = "$" + risk.toFixed(2);
      document.getElementById("out-reward")!.textContent = "$" + reward.toFixed(2);
      document.getElementById("out-ratio")!.textContent = `1 : ${ratio.toFixed(2)}`;
    }
    document.getElementById("calc-form")?.addEventListener("input", calc);
    calc();
  </script>

  <Fragment slot="explanation">
    <h2>How this works</h2>
    <p>
      The risk/reward ratio compares how much you stand to lose if a trade
      hits your stop-loss against how much you stand to gain if it hits your
      take-profit target. A ratio of 1:3 means you're risking one dollar to
      potentially make three.
    </p>
    <p>
      Risk/reward is only half the picture — it needs to be weighed against
      your strategy's actual win rate. A high ratio with a very low win rate
      can still be unprofitable over time, and a lower ratio with a high win
      rate can still work. Neither number alone tells you whether a strategy
      is sound.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
